7. Construction Environmental Management Plan
7.1 The Holder must retain one or more Qualified Professionals to develop a Construction
Environmental Management Plan. The plan must be developed in consultation with
ENV, NH and Indigenous Nations.
7.2 The Construction Environmental Management Plan must include, at a minimum, the
means by which the following will be addressed:
a) dust, light and odour management;
b) sedimentation and erosion control;
c) emergency response and spill prevention;
d) noise management;
e) invasive plants management;
f) stormwater management;
g) surface water management
h) wildlife management;
i) waste management;
j) pre-construction vegetation surveys for identification of vegetation communities and
species composition; and
k) pre-construction surveys and measurers to avoid or mitigate effects for amphibians
and migratory birds during construction.
7.3 The Holder must provide the Construction Environmental Management Plan to the
EAO, ENV, NH and Indigenous Nations for review a minimum of 75 days prior to the
planned commencement of Construction.
7.4 The plan, and any amendments thereto, must be implemented to the satisfaction of a
Qualified Professional throughout Construction and to the satisfaction of the EAO.

8. Operations Environmental Management Plan
8.1 The Holder must retain one or more Qualified Professionals to develop an Operations
Environmental Management Plan. The plan must be developed in consultation with
ENV, NH, and Indigenous Nations.
8.2 The plan must include, at a minimum, the means by which the following will be
addressed:
a) dust, light and odor management;
b) sedimentation and erosion control;
c) emergency response and spill prevention;
d) noise management;
e) invasive plants management;
f) wildlife management;
g) stormwater management;
h) surface water management;
i) site restoration; and,
j) waste management.
8.3 The Holder must provide the Operations Environmental Management Plan to the EAO,
ENV, NH and Indigenous Nations a minimum of 75 days prior to the planned
commencement of Operations.
8.4 The plan, and any amendments thereto, must be implemented to the satisfaction of a
Qualified Professional throughout Operations and to the satisfaction of the EAO.
